erializableAddressBook. Model#hasPerson becomes Model#findConflict, with an overload that excludes the contact being edited, so editing a contact to another contact\u0027s phone or email is no longer silently accepted. All three commands and the data-file loader report the specific ContactConflict message; the generic duplicate messages are removed.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":127,"deletions":72},"test-code":{"insertions":433,"deletions":109}}},{"hash":"840e66adfef23340e157eb4b39177c0531b98263","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Test duplicate-contact rules in storage and end to end","messageBody":"Cover loading files with same-name contacts, clashing phones, case-different emails, clashing Telegram usernames and legacy contacts without Telegram, a same-name save and load round trip, and a rejected add that leaves the model, saved file and undo history unchanged.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"test-code":{"insertions":114,"deletions":10}}},{"hash":"349a838898e07d99becaed1a20450774b82d4353","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Test commands on contacts that share a name","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"test-code":{"insertions":71,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"da627263a45871e4bdd477f8aee7ab9f853f7a68","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Document the duplicate-contact rule","messageBody":"UG: state the rule and the exact rejection messages under add, reference it from edit, and note that a data file breaking it is rejected on load. DG: add a design note with alternatives, add UC05 with a duplicate-details extension, and remove the same-name warning user story.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":81,"deletions":1}}},{"hash":"1fe835388f6fbe19af40278306662703ee06906b","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Back up an unloadable data file before starting empty","messageBody":"A valid JSON file rejected on load (e.g. for duplicate contact details) has no retired fields, so the legacy backup did n